**Why this works:** Moving from row `sr` to row `hr` requires visiting every intermediate row exactly once (costs are non-negative, so backtracking only adds cost). Same for columns. The order of row/column moves doesn't matter since row costs depend only on the destination row and column costs only on the destination column.

**Speedup:** From O(m × n) with a full DP table allocation → O(|Δrow| + |Δcol|) using C-optimized `sum()` on list slices. No grid allocation, no nested loops, no `min()` calls.

